  {"op": "index", "title": "P6-1 rivers past the map edge", "intro": "Produced by tools/render_jobs/jobs/p6_look.json at 1920x1080. _p6_look_forest: a new 150 ft temperate forest map (seed 1234) with a waist river drawn on past the near edge with a bend (its drawn course kept as the river's beyond) and an ankle stream drawn to stop at the right edge (an automatic continuation from the map seed). _p6_look_valley: a new 150 ft temperate forest Valley (seed 2, the recipe's river, whose ends are at the edge). Per exit: home zoom panned to it, zoom 20 and zoom 8 on the mouth, each with fog off and on (density 0.012). Last, the valley under two environment presets with a sky backdrop (outdoor_sunset with its own fog, outdoor_day). Judge: does the river read as going somewhere, any seam at the edge, any bright or dark band where the skirt ends, the fog matched. p6.gd info in log.txt lists the exits."},
